WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Why is it important to report a scam to the FBI and IC3?

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:16.000
The FBI works to protect the public from fraud. If you believe you are a victim, report it to the Internet Crime Complaint Center, IC3.gov.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Reports help us understand trends, identify scam patterns and connect related criminal activity.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:39.000
They also help us warn the public, inform financial institutions and investigate those responsible.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:49.000
We receive about 3,200 cryptocurrency investment fraud complaints each month.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:01:04.000
These scams affect people from every background. Many victims are between 30 and 60 and are comfortable with technology.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:16.000
Operation Level Up is an FBI initiative developed with our partners at the U.S. Secret Service.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:30.000
We identify people being targeted by crypto investment scams, contact them and warn them that the investment is fraudulent.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:43.000
This is a proactive approach: reaching people before they lose more money, rather than responding only after the loss.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:53.000
By intervening early, we can protect people's money—and sometimes save lives.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:02:07.000
If the FBI contacts you, agents will explain how to verify their identity, usually by email or phone.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:20.000
The FBI will never ask you to pay money, move assets to a new account or provide sensitive personal information.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:34.000
Watch for unsolicited texts or social messages, including “wrong-number” messages, that turn into investment pitches.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:47.000
Be cautious when someone you meet online gradually introduces an investment you never planned to make.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:58.000
Do not invest based only on advice from someone you have met online. Never send money to someone you have not met in person.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:09.000
If you think you are being scammed, take a beat. Pause and think before you act.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:21.000
Stop sending money to people you have only met online, and stop communicating with the suspected scammer.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:34.000
Report the fraud to IC3.gov and contact your financial institutions.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:45.000
Talk with someone you trust, such as a family member or loved one.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:35.000
If we can stop even one more investment—or prevent a victim from paying a final “release” fee—we can make a real difference.

